    description: "Found by the WI-mozig premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7. The user taint source loader _load_source_yaml (taint.py:1766-1815) builds only functions: and methods: entries. A user file under taint_sources.d/ or --taint-sources with an attributes: key (e.g. attributes: [location] for document.location) is reported as loaded and contributes nothing, with no warning. Live check: such a file left both affected claims' verdicts identical to baseline. WI-jojis (wont_do) chose auto-derivation from io_primitives for attribute sources, so supporting the key is not required; the minimum is that the loader refuses or warns, naming the ignored key -- a user row that silently does nothing is the 'silent limitation is a defect' case."  # 334a
    fields: {}  # 334a
